  "question": {
    "text": "Which of the following relationship when graphed give a rectangular parabola for helium gas?<br />\rI. KE vs T at constant P and V<br />\rII. V vs <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> at constant P and n<br />\rIII. P vs V at constant T and n"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "III",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "I and III",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "II",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "II and III",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Graph of P vs V at constant T is a rectangular parabola.<br />Graph of V vs <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> at constant P and n is a rectangular parabola.<br />Kinetic energy <math><mo>∝</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math><br />Hence a graph between KE v/s T will be in straight line."
  }
